  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 149,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\cocoartf1138\\cocoasubrtf510\n{\\fonttbl\\f0\\fswiss\\fcharset0 ArialMT;\\f1\\fswiss\\fcharset0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Helvetica;}\n{\\colortbl;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2149,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\paperw12240\\paperh20160\\margl1440\\margr1440\\vieww14260\\viewh17500\\viewkind1\n\\pard\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\pardirnatural"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3149,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\f0\\fs28 \\cf0 Imagine learning for the first\neighteen years of your life that the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4149,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5149,
    "dDurationMs": 2341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All through elementary school and high school\nyou grow up hearing about the flat earth we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7490,
    "dDurationMs": 3469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live on and doing boring flat-earth physics\nhomework and then (if you're lucky enough)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10959,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get to college and PSYCH!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12299,
    "dDurationMs": 4281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\f1 for the first time they show you a globe\nand say \"sorry for lying, the earth is actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16580,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "round\".\\\n\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17580,
    "dDurationMs": 3449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this is, unfortunately, exactly what\nwe do with\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21029,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\\n1) Gravity\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22349,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You probably learned that objects attract\neach other based on their mass so you probably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25890,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grew up thinking that light can't possibly\nbe affected by gravity because light is massless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30080,
    "dDurationMs": 1449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know I did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31529,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well guess what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32529,
    "dDurationMs": 5271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The source of gravity is not mass - it's energy\nand momentum, which light certainly has (of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37800,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "course, regular matter does too)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39610,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So not only does light get bent passing by\na star or planet or black hole, but light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43570,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attracts the planet or star or black hole\nin return (to be sure, it's only a very very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47780,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "small amount."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48780,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a small amount is not zero)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50290,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, the point is that Newton's law of\ngravitation is just an approximation - good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54230,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough to get us to the moon, but not perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56550,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "General relativity is better.\\\n\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58170,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2) Special Relativity\\\nSpeaking of the moon, you probably also learned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61040,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if a sheep is moving 2 mph relative to\na train and that train is moving 2 mph in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65640,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same direction relative to the ground,\nthen the sheep is moving four mph relative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69170,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70590,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2mph+2mph=4mph, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73170,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "FALSE."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74460,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Experiments in special relativity have confirmed\nthat velocities don't simply add together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78190,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so the sheep will in fact be moving very\nvery ever-so-slightly slower than four mph"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82940,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84000,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the formula that correctly predicts this\ndeviation from just adding the velocities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87620,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is (v1+v2)/(1+v1*v2/c^2)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92550,
    "dDurationMs": 3489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not a very big effect, but then again,\nthe earth looks pretty flat, doesn't it?\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96039,
    "dDurationMs": 3261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\\nBut the earth isn't flat: if I walk 10,000km"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99300,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from my cat, and you continue on walking\n10,000km more, you're NOT 20,000km away from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "my cat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105920,
    "dDurationMs": 4809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're just 12,750km away\\'85 in fact, the\nfarthest on earth you can get from ANYTHING"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110729,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on earth is 12,750km."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112229,
    "dDurationMs": 6101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the \"earthly distance-limit\", though\nwe normally call it the diameter of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118330,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And similarly, when you try to add two velocities\ntogether, there's a \"cosmic speed limit\" of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122590,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "300,000,000m/s - that is, the speed of light.\\\n\\"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125900,
    "dDurationMs": 4249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, just because to our eyes the earth looks\nflat, velocities look like they simply add"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130149,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "together, and light looks like it doesn't\nattract gravitationally, is that an excuse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133519,
    "dDurationMs": 23871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to mislead ourselves and our children about\nthe true nature of things?}"
    } ]
  } ]
}
